distrobox-create: fix the read-only volume option on podman+runc

For a read-only top-level directory the option became "ro:rslave", which
podman rejects ("incorrect volume format"): options are comma-separated.
Only hosts with a read-only root (image-based systems) take this path.

Signed-off-by: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
---
--- a/distrobox-create	2026-09-28 20:25:34.704816938 -0400
+++ b/distrobox-create	2026-09-28 20:25:34.707079894 -0400
@@ -751,7 +751,7 @@
 				tr ',' '\n' | grep -q "^ro$"; then
 
 				result_command="${result_command}
-				--volume ${rootdir}:/run/host${rootdir}:ro${rslave}"
+				--volume ${rootdir}:/run/host${rootdir}:ro${rslave:+,rslave}"
 				continue
 			fi
 
